# {{PRODUCT}} Android agent instructions

Read `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md`; it is the authoritative safety contract.

## Daily workflow

- Graph-backed discovery: exact target -> `task-context`; feature/unknown/refactor -> `graph`; search never anchors discovery.
- Do not inspect `.agents/scripts/**` during normal app work.
- Clarify ambiguity and discuss requested edge cases in plain chat before planning. Approved plan required for mutations; approval covers stated phases.
- Unified Chat & Question UI/UX (Language-Adaptive): Match the developer's active conversation language dynamically and use the canonical Markdown cards from `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md` (Plan Approval Card, Reviewer Dispatch Table `| Reviewer | Model | Status |`, Review Verdict Table `| Reviewer | Model | Verdict | Findings |`, 3-Section Mobile Walkthrough, Commit Card, and `ask_question` modals). On partial reviewer completion, output at most one short progress line (e.g. `1/3`). In any RTL language, start every line/bullet with a word in that language and wrap code symbols, file names, commands, and English terms in `` `backticks` ``.
- After approval, execute phases autonomously. Follow-ups within active scope must execute immediately: never generate redundant plan artifacts or stall for nonexistent UI buttons (record in-scope refinements via `task plan-note` before `prepare-verification`).
- Policy evaluates 6 risk tiers (`T0_TRIVIAL` to `T5_CRITICAL`) as runtime authority for gates, reviewers, and device.
- Query `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task status --task-id <id> --next` for canonical next actions.
- Verification order: preflight -> tests -> routed reviews -> assemble/device -> Mobile Verification Walkthrough and sign-off -> final verification.
- Never self-certify HIGH/CRITICAL reviews with `record_review.py --verdict PASS`. Adjudicate false positives via `validate-finding`. Never poll background work (Zero-Polling invariant).
- Context notes are administrative: clarify ambiguity first, then translate into English before running `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py context note "<structured-english-note>"`. Always follow `.agents/project-context/project-notes.md`.

## Canonical Command Catalog

| Step | Command |
|---|---|
| Task context | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task-context --file <path> --json` |
| Feature / find graph | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py graph --feature <name> --json` |
| Task status | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task status --task-id <id> --next` |
| Context note | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py context note "<structured-english-note>"` (`--replace "<old>"` / `--remove "<old>"`) |
| Preflight | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py preflight` |
| Unit tests | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py test` |
| Review evidence | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review complete --task <id> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` -> `review finalize --task <id>` |
| Resume | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task resume --task-id <id>` |
| Assemble | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble` |
| Device | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py device install-start` |
| Verify | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py verify --task-id <id>` |

